Implement CSS. Need write selectors. Ensure token usage.

CSS:
```
/* ===== Slider ===== */
.pathland-slider { display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:.625rem; }
.pathland-slider input[type='range'] {
  -webkit-appearance:none;
  appearance:none;
  flex:1;
  min-width:0;
  height:1.25rem;
  margin:0;
  background:transparent;
  cursor:pointer;
  accent-color:var(--pl-slider-accent);
  --pl-slider-fill:0%;
}
.pathland-slider input[type='range']::-webkit-slider-runnable-track {
  height:.375rem;
  border-radius:9999px;
  background: linear-gradient(to right, var(--pl-slider-accent) 0%, var(--pl-slider-accent) var(--pl-slider-fill), var(--pl-slider-track) var(--pl-slider-fill), var(--pl-slider-track) 100%);
}
... thumb
```
Thumb:
```
.pathland-slider input[type='range']::-webkit-slider-thumb {
 -webkit-appearance:none; appearance:none;
 width:1rem; height:1rem; margin-top:-.3125rem;
 border-radius:9999px;
 background:var(--pl-slider-thumb);
 border:1px solid var(--pl-slider-track);
 box-shadow: var(--pl-elevation-low-x) var(--pl-elevation-low-y) var(--pl-elevation-low-blur) var(--pl-elevation-low-radius) var(--pl-elevation-low-color);
}
```
Firefox track/progress/thumb:
```
::-moz-range-track { height:.375rem; border-radius...; background:var(--pl-slider-track); }
::-moz-range-progress { height:.375rem; border-radius...; background:var(--pl-slider-accent); }
::-moz-range-thumb { width:1rem; height:1rem; border-radius:9999px; background:var(--pl-slider-thumb); border:1px solid var(--pl-slider-track); box-shadow:...; }
```
Note `-moz-range-progress` auto fill; our gradient for WebKit; we set var for both perhaps. Fine.
Focus:
```
.pathland-slider input[type='range']:focus-visible { outline:2px solid var(--pl-slider-accent); outline-offset:4px; border-radius:9999px; }
```
Maybe the outline around input entire width; okay. Could set `outline-offset:2px`.
Disabled:
```
.pathland-slider input[type='range']:disabled { cursor:default; opacity:var(--pl-opacity-disabled); }
```

Hover/active thumb could use `filter: brightness` but no need. Maybe transition thumb? Pseudo element transitions work:
```
::...-thumb { transition: box-shadow 120ms; }
```
Not needed.

Apply CSS.

